 "relevance_note": "Single-patient case report of a girl with CdLS and pustular psoriasis carrying 'a heterozygous variant of uncertain significance in TNFAIP3' (c.2199C>A, p.(Cys733*)).",
 "method_note": "Read whole paper manually; small Python script only assembled the JSON (no table transcription). One in-scope person: the single unnamed proband, labelled 'patient' (rule 5; 'the proband' is a role word). Not given rows: the mother ('a maternal history of cleft palate' - not described as tested or affected by an HA20-related condition, and it is unclear the phrase refers to the mother herself); previously published CdLS+psoriasis cases (Lubkov 2018, Mugheddu 2020, Pakistan case) have no TNFAIP3 variant or HA20 diagnosis, so out of scope. RAD21 variant recorded as a second variant row (attributed unambiguously to the patient). Contradictions/inconsistencies: (1) Figures 2 and 3 legends call both variants 'de novo', but no parental testing is described anywhere, so inheritance is 'not reported' (rule 8); (2) RAD21 transcript printed as both NM_006265.2 and 'Transcript: NM_006265.1' - recorded NM_006265.2; (3) RAD21 location printed as 'chr8:10,673,499–10,658,686' in text and 'chromosome 8: position 116,852,561 (GRCh38/hg38)' in Figure 2 legend - recorded the latter; (4) RAD21 classification stated as 'likely pathogenic' (Results 2.1), 'probably pathogenic' (2.2.1) and 'pathogenic for CdLS type 4' (Abstract) - recorded likely pathogenic; (5) the TNFAIP3 transcript also printed as Ensembl 'ENST00000612899.5'; (6) the local skin biopsy 'revealed findings compatible with pemphigus foliaceus', whereas later histopathology 'confirmed the diagnosis of pustular psoriasis'; (7) the physical-exam wording 'upper-limb reduction defects that range from subtle phalangeal abnormalities to oligodactyly' repeats the Introduction's general CdLS description and is absent from the Methods exam paragraph - recorded as observed as printed, but uncertain. TNFAIP3 functional evidence left 'not reported': only in-silico AlphaFold modelling and UniProt viewer, no assay; the GEO expression analysis is not about this variant. Neurocognitive features (dysprosody, limited social interaction) recorded as features but the checklist item 'central nervous system involvement' left not reported. Growth failure checklist marked observed from short stature and low weight-for-age. Age 13 years recorded as age at last evaluation (age at presentation); onset age not stated (only an '8-month history'). No ACMG codes, treatment, vital status or consanguinity reported.",
